thub.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/102580","id":2646023290,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6dtxx6","user":{"login":"Hilderin","id":81109165,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMTA5MTY1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81109165?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hilderin","html_url":"https://github.com/Hilderin","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hilderin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hilderin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hilderin/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hilderin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hilderin/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hilderin/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hilderin/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hilderin/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Hilderin/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-09T01:58:44Z","updated_at":"2025-02-09T01:58:44Z","body":"After some testing on Fedora 41+Gnome on Wayland, I find out that any second window (ex: opening the script editor in a second window) causes serious lags in Godot. This issue is also reproductible on Godot 4.3 stable. All I have to do to reproduce it is to open the script editor in a separate window and try to move a Sprite in the 2D editor with the mouse.\n\nI think the issue could be related to Fedora 41 and Wayland. I also see a couple of posts on Fedora forum talking about lags on Wayland since Fedora 41.\n\n@carringtonevent Can you test Godot 4.3 stable and 4.4 beta 3 with an empty project and the script editor on a separate window to see if you have the same result as me?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2646023290/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"ho